# Hollowlike: character dialogue, English.
# One file per language and feature: localization/<language>/<feature>.po.
# Lines start DLG_<CHARACTER>_, names NPC_. msgstr is the text shown; each
# line fills the dialogue box, so keep it to a sentence or two. See
# localization/README.md.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: en\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"

#. Names on the dialogue box's name plate.
msgid "NPC_GUARD"
msgstr "Security Guard"

msgid "NPC_WORKER"
msgstr "Maintenance Worker"

#. The security guard, before you've beaten the Warden. Night shift, nervous,
#. stuck at his post near the start. The "loading bay" is the Warden's arena.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_1"
msgstr "Whoa, easy there. Didn't think anyone still came down here."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_2"
msgstr "Night shift's been quiet since the lights went out. Too quiet."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_3"
msgstr "Something's holed up in the old loading bay past the shutter. Big. Armoured. I'd turn back if I were you."

#. The guard, before the Warden, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_BEFORE_AGAIN"
msgstr "Still here? That thing in the loading bay isn't going anywhere. Neither am I."

#. The guard, after you've beaten the Warden: thanks, and a warning about the
#. Sin Hawk (the bird boss), which nests high up past the climb.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_1"
msgstr "You took that thing down? I... thank you. Really."

#. The guard hands you a Strong Pipe (a heavier weapon), right after thanking you.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_GIFT"
msgstr "Here, take this. Found it on my rounds. Hits a lot harder than that rusty thing."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_2"
msgstr "But listen. Up past the climb, the Sin Hawk's nesting in the rafters. Feathers like knives."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_3"
msgstr "It sees you long before you see it. Keep moving, and watch the sky."

#. The guard, after the Warden, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_WARDEN_AGAIN"
msgstr "Thanks again. And mind the rafters."

#. The guard, after you've beaten the Sin Hawk too.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_1"
msgstr "Both of them? You're something else."

msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_2"
msgstr "Maybe I'll finally get some quiet on this shift."

#. The guard, after the Sin Hawk, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_GUARD_AFTER_HARRIER_AGAIN"
msgstr "Quiet nights from here on. I hope."

#. The maintenance worker, resting by the bench at the Span's near end. Tired,
#. dry, kind. Before the Warden (you can't normally get here then).
msgid "DLG_WORKER_BEFORE_1"
msgstr "How'd you get up here? Never mind. Mind the pits."

msgid "DLG_WORKER_BEFORE_AGAIN"
msgstr "Still here. Still on break."

#. After the Warden: you crossed the Junction's gap with the dash. Points the
#. way to the Sin Hawk's nest, and says to rest at the bench first.
msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_WARDEN_1"
msgstr "You jumped that gap? Nobody's come over that gap in weeks."

msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_WARDEN_2"
msgstr "The far door's where the Sin Hawk nests. I used to service the fans in there."

msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_WARDEN_3"
msgstr "Sit on that bench before you go. Trust me."

#. After the Warden, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_WARDEN_AGAIN"
msgstr "Bench first. Then the bird."

#. After the Sin Hawk: you can wall jump now. Hints at the two places it opens:
#. the shaft in this room's ceiling, and the wall by the Entrance.
msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_HAWK_1"
msgstr "It's quiet in there. You did that?"

msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_HAWK_2"
msgstr "With spurs like those you could climb the shaft above us. Something shiny's been up there for years."

msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_HAWK_3"
msgstr "And the old vault, up the wall by the way in. The door's been out of reach since the stairs came down."

#. After the Sin Hawk, on every later visit.
msgid "DLG_WORKER_AFTER_HAWK_AGAIN"
msgstr "The shaft above us, and the vault by the way in. Go on."
